# Client environment (Vite)

# Leave VITE_API_URL unset (recommended). The app then calls same-origin `/api`:
#   - local: Vite proxies it to http://localhost:4000 (see vite.config.js)
#   - Vercel: api/[[...path]].js forwards it to the Railway API (Vercel env var API_ORIGIN)
# This keeps login cookies first-party, which iPhone Safari requires.
#
# Only set this to call Railway directly from the browser (cookies become third-party,
# so Safari on iPhone will not keep users logged in). With or without trailing /api:
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-service.up.railway.app
